# Admin language (English default, Italian optional)

The **public site** stays English. The **Payload admin** UI is English by default, with **Italiano** as a second language.

Do **not** enable Payload `localization` / `localized: true`. Admin language is copy + `i18n`, not content locales.

## English (unchanged)

- Field `label` (and array/block row labels that name a field): `Name`, `Year`, `Show site banner`, `Title`.
- Select option labels that match stored values: `Info`, `Change`, `Urgent`, `Primary Investigator`.
- Block type labels in the picker (`Accordion`, `Content`) when they name the block slug.

Editors match the English name to the field. The handbook quotes those names as they appear.

## Bilingual chrome (`copy(en, it)` / `t('fcr:…')`)

- Payload chrome: `i18n.fallbackLanguage: 'en'` and `supportedLanguages: { en, it }` (import `en` and `it` from `payload/i18n`).
- Collection/global `labels`, `admin.group`, tab labels, `admin.description` as `{ en, it }` via `@/i18n/copy`.
- Custom admin components, toasts, confirms, validation messages: `req.t('fcr:…')` or `useTranslation()`.
- Dashboard cards and custom nav (`Site` / **Sito**, **Active conference** / **Conferenza attiva**, **Conference archive** / **Archivio conferenze**, ungrouped **Edit active edition** / **Modifica edizione attiva**, publishing guide).

```ts
// ✅ field name English, help bilingual
{ name: 'year', label: 'Year', admin: { description: copy('Edition year. Several editions in the same year are allowed.', 'Anno dell’edizione. Più edizioni nello stesso anno sono ammesse.') } }

// ❌ do not translate the field name
{ name: 'year', label: 'Anno', admin: { description: 'Edition year.' } }
```

When a custom component mentions a field, keep the **English field label** inside the sentence (`Show site banner`, `Send push`).
